## 6. Parameter File

### General rules
1) Every line starts with `:wycfg`.  
2) Max **128 chars** per line (comments count).  
3) All strings **in quotes** (≤ 30 chars).  
4) Use `#` for inline comments.

### Example parameter file
```txt
:wycfg dst[0] 10.10.10.10 65534        # User application server
:wycfg dst[9] "none" 65535             # Xirgo device manager
:wycfg apn[0] "APN.internet" "user" "pass"
:wycfg pcr[0] 00080104030607080b17     # Packet recipe
:wycfg pcr[1] 01050103070809
:wycfg pcr[2] 02140104535455565758595a5b5c5d5e5f6061622c2e
:wycfg tmr[0] 90 1
:wycfg aet[0] 0 1000 1000 205          # Harsh accel thresholds
```

> See **Appendix E** for the complete parameter index. Selected entries:

#### Selected parameters (illustrative subset)
| Name | Indexing / Form | Meaning (ranges) |
|---|---|---|
| `dst[x] <ip> <port>` | `x: 0–9` | Destination servers (`none` for disabled) |
| `apn[x] "<apn>" "<user>" "<pass>"` | GSM only | APN credentials |
| `pcr[x] <hex>` | `x: 0–127` | Packet recipe, see §7 and Appendix F |
| `tmr[x] <secs> <auto_restart>` | `x:0–31` | SW timers for script |
| `aet[x] <mode> <thr1> <thr2> <dur>` | accel events | Thresholds for harsh events |
